    {
        "content": "<p>Few days ago, an <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783\">ArXiv paper</a> showing a sub-quadratic algorithm for 3SUM was published with a <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/main/3sum-apsp\">formalization</a>.<br>\nI was overwhelmed by the news, but I also realized that tweaking a few parameters might improve the time complexity.<br>\nSince I was also interested in showing off a fully-autoformalized project, I just gave some insights to Claude, and it eventually did improve the time complexity, from <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2.99942</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{O}(n^{2.99942})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2.99942</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> in the original paper to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2.99791</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{O}(n^{2.99791})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2.99791</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> for APSP, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>1.9992</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{O}(n^{1.9992})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.9992</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>1.99896</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{O}(n^{1.99896})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1.99896</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> for 3SUM.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/qawbecrdtey/ImprovedExponents\">https://github.com/qawbecrdtey/ImprovedExponents</a></p>\n<p>This couldn't have been done without the authors of the original paper, Alman and Vassilevska Williams.</p>",
        "id": 629794643,
        "sender_full_name": "Jihoon Hyun",
        "timestamp": 1791366682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It now got a <a href=\"https://palomar-registry.org/entry?id=PALOMAR-2026-10-08-000003&amp;version=1\">Palomar registry</a>.<br>\nThe accompanying paper can be checked <a href=\"https://github.com/qawbecrdtey/ImprovedExponents/blob/v4.35.0-rc2/papers/improved-exponents/main.pdf\">here</a>, in the same repository.</p>",
        "id": 630042391,
        "sender_full_name": "Jihoon Hyun",
        "timestamp": 1791441114
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’ve been trying to coordinate improvements to these exponents here:  <a href=\"https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent\">https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent</a> and <a href=\"https://prove2.me/campaigns/3sum-exponent\">https://prove2.me/campaigns/3sum-exponent</a> . Maybe we can work together and lower them further.</p>",
